course: dictionary
lesson: 14189
title: Names, brands and special words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words start with a capital letter because they name one special thing, such as a person, a place, a brand or a group. This is a proper noun. «Maria Moro came to our school to talk about her job.» Here Moro is a family name, the surname of one person and her family.
explain: Context helps you to know what kind of Moro is meant. «I bought a Moro bar at the shop in Auckland.» The shop, the bar and the city tell you Moro is a chocolate bar sold in New Zealand, not a person's name.
explain: In a medical leaflet, the Moro reflex is a startle movement. «The nurse showed us the baby's Moro reflex: her arms flew out when she felt she was falling.» Look at the clues: a newborn baby, a sudden startle, arms thrown out, and falling. Those clues tell you what the reflex is.
fact: A proper noun is the name of one particular person, place, brand or group, and it starts with a capital letter.
fact: «Moro» is a family name (surname) in Italian, Spanish and other languages.
fact: «Moro» is also a chocolate bar sold in New Zealand and Australia.
fact: The Moro reflex is a startle movement a newborn baby makes, throwing out its arms when it feels it is falling.
fact: «The Moro» can also name Muslim peoples of the southern Philippines.
exercise: «Maria Moro is our new class helper.» What kind of word is Moro here? | *A family name (surname) | A number | A colour | A verb meaning to run
exercise: «The Moro reflex makes a newborn baby throw out its arms.» What does the Moro reflex show? | A baby learning to walk | A baby laughing at a toy | *A startle movement when a baby feels it is falling | A baby sleeping soundly
exercise: «Dad bought a Moro bar in Sydney.» What is a Moro in this sentence? | A type of bus | A kind of bird | *A chocolate bar | A river in Italy
test: «The Moro bar was sold in a shop in Wellington.» Where was it sold? | Japan | *New Zealand | Canada | Spain
test: The nurse said the baby's Moro was normal. What does the nurse mean? | A sleepy yawn | *The newborn's startle reflex, with arms thrown out | The baby's name | The baby's first word
exam: Which word is a proper noun, a special name that starts with a capital letter? | *Moro | arms | reflex | baby
